{
  "summary":"Intermittent DNS resolution failures between services; nslookup commands show inability to resolve 'kubernetes.default', indicating a CoreDNS or DNS configuration issue.",
  "likely_cause":"CoreDNS add‑on problem or misconfigured DNS settings (e.g., incorrect nameserver or search path in /etc/resolv.conf) causing intermittent name resolution failures.",
  "confidence":"medium",
  "next_action":"kubectl exec -ti dnsutils -- cat /etc/resolv.conf to verify nameserver and search path; run nslookup from dnsutils pod to reproduce errors; check CoreDNS pod status (kubectl get pods -n kube-system -l k8s-app=kube-dns); inspect CoreDNS logs (kubectl logs -n kube-system <coredns-pod>); if pods are unhealthy or logs show errors, restart or redeploy CoreDNS; ensure kubelet --cluster-dns flag matches CoreDNS service IP."
}
